{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2956","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2956","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2956\",\"parent_revision\":\"b5ee2fdb2375de6a4ed7917e6673d9fcfdb2c536a89706e7c28a0c9130577ada\",\"root_revision\":\"b5ee2fdb2375de6a4ed7917e6673d9fcfdb2c536a89706e7c28a0c9130577ada\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P0\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEvery `backlog_groom` call made during a grooming pass on #2953 and #2955 (16+ calls across 6 different agents plus the orchestrator, spanning two separate GitHub-backend items) returned `\\\"groomed_updated\\\": true` with zero errors, but none of the written content was retrievable afterward through `backlog_view` \u2014 via CLI or MCP, `summary=true` or `summary=false`. `sections_index` continued showing only the item's original 4 sections. Cross-checked directly against the live GitHub issue (`gh api repos/.../issues/{N}`): `updated_at` predated the entire grooming session, confirming nothing reached GitHub either.\\n\\nThe content was not lost \u2014 it exists in the local cache file (`~/.dh/projects/{slug}/github-cache/items/issues/{N}.yaml`), but under roughly 3x the expected number of top-level section keys. Two distinct patterns observed in the cache:\\n1. Duplication \u2014 a section written under its correct name (e.g. `Files`, `Resources`, `Impact`, `Impact Radius`, `Dependencies`, `Priority`, `Benefits`, `Research`, `Design Intent Alignment`, `Acceptance Criteria`, `Expected Behavior`) also appears a second time under an `unknown__{slug}` key with the same content.\\n2. Case/format mangling with no canonical counterpart at all \u2014 `RT-ICA` was stored only as `rt_ica`, `Fact-Check` only as `fact_check`, `Issue Classification` only as `issue_classification`; none exist under their documented Title-Case/hyphenated names anywhere in the file.\\n3. Per-claim fact-checker writes fragmented into separate top-level sections instead of one `Fact-Check` section (`unknown__claim_1:_\\\"...\\\"`, `unknown__claim_3:_\\\"...\\\"`, etc., with the full claim text embedded in the YAML key itself).\\n4. Even sections nobody touched this session (`Story`, `Context`) acquired `unknown__` duplicates.\\n\\nA follow-up investigation (2026-08-18) traced this to `_normalize_section_key()` in `backlog_core/operations.py` (canonical `SECTION_HEADING` map covers only 3 entries: `fact_check`, `rt_ica`, `issue_classification`; any other section name passes through unchanged on write) combined with `parse_issue_body()` in `backlog_core/github_sync.py` (any heading not in that same 3-entry map gets bucketed as `unknown__{slug}` on re-parse instead of matched back to the key it was just written under) \u2014 plus a separate, not-yet-fully-diagnosed failure in the GitHub push/replay path that means pending mutations never actually reach the live issue. Full diagnosis with file:line citations: `/private/tmp/claude-503/-Users-jamienelson-repos-claude-skills/2da56558-aee9-4992-9946-ab27b7af9cbb/scratchpad/reports/20260818-backlog-groom-visibility-bug.md`.\\n\\nImpact: any item groomed through the GitHub backend via `backlog_groom` with non-canonical section names \u2014 i.e. essentially every real grooming pass \u2014 silently produces an unreadable, duplicated section structure that never reaches the actual GitHub issue, while every tool call in the chain reports success. `mark_groomed=True` would advance the item's status label while its real content stays effectively empty to any consumer. This has been running unnoticed across many prior grooming sessions.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 discovered live while grooming #2953 via /dh:work-backlog-item, confirmed via root-cause investigation 2026-08-18\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **backlog_groom writes report success but are invisible via backlog_view \u2014 section-key duplication in _normalize_section_key plus broken github sync replay** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ca9bc5b50628d44cd7eafec7c95b2c90f4efcdc0a0f062691d3a66a6f35c2688\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTbn-Q\"}"}